INSERT INTO "Requirement_Item__c" VALUES('Requirement_Item__c-665','True','False','True','','Started App','','','2023-08-09T17:23:48.000+0000','Doctoral','','3.0','True','True','Started App','','','','','','','','<center><b><Font size=4 Font color=#6d3696>Professional/Academic Portfolio</b></Font><Font color=Red>*</Font></center>

<br>

<br>

If you have not taken the GRE or MAT, and do not plan to take one of these accepted admissions assessments, you may choose to submit a digital portfolio. If you choose this option, the following elements are required to complete your digital portfolio:

<br>

<br>

Five to seven electronic artifacts illustrating your accomplishments as an educational leader. Please include a statement explaining why you selected each artifact, and describe how the artifact demonstrates your ability/accomplishments as an educational leader in K-12, Higher Education or Adult Education. Examples to consider including in your portfolio:

<br>

<br>

* Copy of a brochure inviting people to attend a seminar you planned. Describe the purpose of the seminar and how the seminar helped to support student/adult learning in your school or workplace.

<br>

* Video clip of a presentation made before a professional group. Include the reason for the presentation, material used and the goals accomplished. You might also submit a

<br>

* An article published in an academic or community journal/newspaper.

<br>

The artifacts should demonstrate your most effective work as a leader in your field.

<br>

<br>

Please upload a document to answer the following essay question(s). File must be a MS Word (.doc or .docx), Rich Text Format (.rtf), Text (.txt) or PDF (.pdf) document, and not exceed 4 MB.<i> Please be advised, PDF file format uploads are strongly recommended as other file formats may be altered during the upload process.  </i>','','False','False','Professional/Academic Portfolio','2025-04-11T02:55:19.000+0000','','Professional/Academic Portfolio Doct(GSOEd)','','','','012DS00000AdtxiYAB','','','','','','','','Started App','ReqItemUuid-94d254c8-4eb1-422f-9e14-79b4dc269847','','','','True','','','Requirement__c-216');
INSERT INTO "Requirement_Item__c" VALUES('Requirement_Item__c-666','True','False','True','','Started App','','','2023-08-09T17:23:48.000+0000','','','2.0','True','True','Started App','','','ED_EL_EDS|ELPR;ED_EL_EDS|ESEA;ED_EL_EDS|SADI','','','','','<center><b><Font size=4 Font color=#6d3696>Personal Statement</b></Font><Font color=Red>*</Font></center>

<br>

<br>

The mission of the University of St. Thomas School of Education is to educate practitioners to be: 1. morally responsible leaders, who 2. think critically, 3. act wisely, and 4. work skillfully, 5. to advance the common good. In the context of the Mission, please share your experience with discussing sensitive information with a parent/guardian, colleague, or administrator. What strategies did you use to create a positive conversation and arrive at a resolution or plan for moving forward? What have you learned from these encounters, and how has your learning shaped your approach for future encounters? Your response should not be less than 500 words, and not exceed 750 words.

<br>

<br>

Please upload a document to answer the following essay question(s). File must be a MS Word (.doc or .docx), Rich Text Format (.rtf), Text (.txt) or PDF (.pdf) document, and not exceed 4 MB.<i> Please be advised, PDF file format uploads are strongly recommended as other file formats may be altered during the upload process.  </i>','','False','False','Personal Statement','2025-04-11T02:55:19.000+0000','','Personal Statement - Ed Lead - Sped (GSOEd)','','','','012DS00000AdtxiYAB','','','','','','','','Started App','ReqItemUuid-0aff40fd-0b69-4b5f-9f2b-2b4032e2d104','','','','True','','','Requirement__c-216');
